    <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
    <h1>Hi, I’m Giacomo.</h1>
    <p class="subtitle">AI Research Engineer, writing as giacolees.</p>
    <p>My work focuses on computer vision, sensor fusion, and perception for autonomous driving. I also build with language models and explore agentic AI, with an interest in what it takes to turn a promising idea into a useful system.</p>
    <p>This blog is where I work through the things I build and learn. Writing helps me connect the underlying theory to the choices that matter in an implementation: how data is represented, where computation happens, and which tradeoffs shape the result.</p>
    <h2>What I write about</h2>
    <p>You’ll find explanations of machine learning methods, implementations from first principles, and notes on making code run efficiently. Recent articles cover <a href="/posts/tokenizers/">building a tokenizer</a>, <a href="/posts/hardware-aware-programming-for-dummies/">programming with the hardware in mind</a>, <a href="/posts/rl_intro/">reinforcement learning</a>, and <a href="/posts/radiance-fields/">NeRF and Gaussian Splatting</a>.</p>
    <p>I aim to make the reasoning explicit, from the basic concepts to the details that are easy to miss when putting them into practice. These posts are also a record I can return to as my understanding develops.</p>
